From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 14:42:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 120/151] Markdown shortcuts panel

A context drawer page lists every Markdown key, grouped as Text,
Headings, Lists, Tables and Blocks, with keycaps from the key_bind
constants (a test checks that every Markdown binding is listed).
It opens with F1, View > Markdown shortcuts... and a Show button in
Settings > Markdown. The panel leaves the editor focused, so typing and
shortcuts work while it is open. With Vim bindings the keys the editor
handles itself are dimmed.

Escape in the editor with nothing to cancel (no selection, Vim bindings
off) now reaches the app, so it closes the find bar first and then the
drawer; before, the editor always took it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

